        "title": "Stonework: Ashlar, Rubble, Dry-Stone, and Quarrying",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Stone masonry spans an enormous range: from highly engineered, precision-cut ashlar in classical temples to unmodified field stone piled dry in a pasture wall. The structural principles remain the same (compression, interlocking, gravity), but the skill and tooling required vary by an order of magnitude."
